WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.000
About 600 million years ago, the rock that is now Nigeria lay inside a growing supercontinent called Gondwana.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.583
Then South America and Africa pulled apart like a zip opening from the south.

3
00:00:09.583 --> 00:00:10.000
The rift spread north from about 150 or 140 million years ago, and new ocean floor formed from about 135 to 130 million years ago.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.483
Around 900 BCE settlements suddenly became much denser, and people began making large clay sculptures of human heads and figures.

5
00:00:13.483 --> 00:00:15.000
Many were deliberately broken and deposited, some near graves, at sites such as Pangwari and Ifana.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.667
In the later part of this phase, Nok people built furnaces and smelted iron, among the earliest iron working known in West Africa.

7
00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:20.000
Iron came a few centuries after the first terracottas, so the two should not be treated as one package.
